{"availability":"available","full":"Eshanya1/pr-review-agent","name":"pr-review-agent","description":"Multi-agent PR reviewer with a critic pass that verifies every finding against the diff before escalating to a human. Zero-setup demo (no API key) + 15-fixture eval harness with real precision/recall numbers.","category":"Design","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-19T19:32:44Z","updated":"2026-09-03T17:09:29Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["ai-agents","anthropic","code-review","llm","portfolio-project","python","security","static-analysis"],"demo":"https://eshanya1.github.io/pr-review-agent/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T07:32:33.305Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T07:32:33.305Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T07:32:33.305Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T06:44:33.421Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T07:32:33.305Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Try it instantly → — loads immediately, no build wait, replays all 15 real eval fixtures client-side with the actual diff, findings, and verifier decision from both the cassette and a validated live run (88.0% F1, reproduced identically 3 times).","[]( — for the real CLI in a real terminal instead: no install, opens a real terminal with the tool already set up. Run pr-review-agent eval once it loads (takes 1-2 min to build the first time).","A multi-agent system with two capabilities over the same repo: PR review (reviewer agent → critic that verifies every claim against the diff → escalation policy) and RAG Q&A (ask natural-language questions about the codebase, answered only from retrieved chunks, cited). Both are wrapped in the same guardrails (structured-output validation, prompt-injection scanning) and the same self-built observability (latency, tokens, estimated cost per call — no external account needed)."],"features":["Evidence found in the diff → finding stays at full confidence, marked verified.","Evidence not found (hallucinated, paraphrased, wrong file) → confidence is"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Eshanya1/pr-review-agent/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"668f3263fbb36356f6bc9c995441ca56f1069d4c87aff683702cae8f320c5264","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:33.628Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T06:44:33.628Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Try it instantly → — loads immediately, no build wait, replays all 15 real eval fixtures client-side with the actual diff, findings, and verifier decision from both the cassette and a validated live run (88.0% F1, reproduced identically 3 times).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Eshanya1/pr-review-agent/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"not_required","text":"Both are wrapped in the same guardrails (structured-output validation, prompt-injection scanning) and the same self-built observability (latency, tokens, estimated cost per call — no external account needed).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Eshanya1/pr-review-agent/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"At the scale of one repo's chunks (hundreds, not millions) an ANN index would be premature, and this needs no hosted database, no account, no native SQLite extension to load (I tried sqlite-vec first — it needs SQLite's extension-loading enabled, which this machine's Python build doesn't have; rather than risk that being a \"works on my laptop\" trap again, NumPy won).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Eshanya1/pr-review-agent/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"not_required","text":"No external account, no network call needed to see your own cost/latency history.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Eshanya1/pr-review-agent/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"668f3263fbb36356f6bc9c995441ca56f1069d4c87aff683702cae8f320c5264","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Eshanya1/pr-review-agent/blob/main/README.md","chec